  "$comment": "Feed registry for the news synthesiser. Tiers follow the brief: tier 1 is the live pulse, tier 2 is depth and corroboration, tier 3 is institutional context. Adding a feed is a config change.",
  "$agencyNote": "The wire agencies no longer publish open feeds — Reuters returns 404, AP requires a licence, AFP has none. Their reporting still reaches us second-hand through GDELT and through the outlets below, but no feed here should be labelled as a wire. The live-pulse tier is therefore carried by international broadcasters.",
  "$blockedNote": "Probed and rejected as unreachable to an automated client: ISW, IMF, OECD, UNCTAD and Chatham House all return 403 to any user agent; the World Bank newsroom serves HTML rather than a feed. The GDELT article API was also rejected: it rate-limits to one request per five seconds and refused even at seven, which is too unreliable for a scheduled run.",
